---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro'
---
<Doc title="Curriculum Vitae, access controlled" description="Section 6. The resume is issued on a signed link with a 24 hour life rather than served as a page.">
  <div class="mast">
    <div>Off the Bit
<b>Section 6: Curriculum Vitae</b>
Category: Informational
Access: CONTROLLED</div>
    <div class="r"><b>M. Imran</b>
Token lifetime: 86400 s
24 hour life, revocable
X-Robots-Tag: noindex</div>
  </div>
  <div class="title">
    <h1>6. Curriculum Vitae</h1>
    <div class="sub">Access controlled, for reasons that are about other people's privacy rather than about mine</div>
  </div>
  <h2 id="s61">6.1. Rationale</h2>
  <div class="ind prose">
    <p>Sections 3 through 5 of the index draft are a more useful record than any résumé. They carry numbers, named
    failures, revision dates, and claims you can check against people who were in the room.</p>
    <p>The document itself carries client names, reference contacts and a phone number that belong to other
    people's privacy as much as to my convenience. So it goes out on a signed link rather than sitting at a
    guessable path in a public bucket.</p>
  </div>
  <h2 id="s62">6.2. Request</h2>
  <div class="ind">
    <div class="gate">
      <div class="ep">POST /api/cv</div>
      <form method="post" action="/api/cv">
        <label class="skip" for="cv-email">Email address</label>
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label for="cv-company">Company</label>
          <input id="cv-company" type="text" name="company" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
        </div>
        <input id="cv-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@company.com" autocomplete="email" required>
        <button type="submit">Request link</button>
      </form>
      <p class="fine">Returns <code>202 Accepted</code> and mails a signed link, openable more than once inside 24 hours. Time to live
      86400 seconds. Rate limited to three per address per day and sixty per source network per
      hour. Your address goes to the access log in 6.4 and nowhere else, is never added to a list,
      and is deleted the same day you ask.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h2 id="s65">6.5. Alternatives</h2>
  <div class="ind">
    <table class="rt">
      <thead><tr><th style="width:110px">Preference</th><th>Path</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr><td class="hd" data-l="Preference">Preferred</td><td data-l="Path">Write to <a href="mailto:hey@mosthofaimran.com">hey@mosthofaimran.com</a> and say what the role is.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="hd" data-l="Preference">Fine</td><td data-l="Path">Use the form in 6.2.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="hd" data-l="Preference">Also fine</td><td data-l="Path">Do not request it at all. Sections 3 through 5 will tell you more about how I work.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <h2 id="s66">6.6. Who else processes this</h2>
  <div class="ind">
    <p class="dim" style="max-width:80ch">A privacy claim that lists what I keep, and not who else
    holds it, covers half the problem. Slack joins this table the day it is switched on and not
    before: the code shipped on 2026-09-03 and does nothing until a webhook is set.</p>
    <table class="rt">
      <thead><tr><th style="width:150px">Processor</th><th style="width:200px">What it sees</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      <tr><td class="hd" data-l="Processor">Cloudflare</td><td data-l="Sees">Every request, and a page-view beacon in your browser</td><td data-l="Why">Hosting, the token store, the file. Web Analytics is on, so a third-party script loads on every page. Section 10 has the cost</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="hd" data-l="Processor">Resend</td><td data-l="Sees">Your address and the link</td><td data-l="Why">Delivering the mail. There is no other way to send you one</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>Imran</span><span>Section 6, access controlled</span><span>[Page 8]</span></div>
</Doc>
